From 2c5dd0b3c4b54ff0d842b3cfb9d1d939ec3fb6a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Lee <yowching.lee@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avoid c23 nodiscard spelling

GCC on newer Debian testing systems accepts the C23-style
[[__nodiscard__]] spelling, but GNU m4 1.4.19's bundled gnulib places
_GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD before the return type in several inline
definitions. That placement is valid for GCC's warn_unused_result
attribute form, but not for [[__nodiscard__]], causing builds to fail in
gl_oset.h.

Prefer the GNU attribute spelling when it is available and only fall back
to the C23-style spelling otherwise. Patch only the release tarball's
generated config header template so bootstrap builds do not need
maintainer tools such as aclocal.
---
 lib/config.hin | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/config.hin b/lib/config.hin
index 8d7b24c..75171de 100644
--- a/lib/config.hin
+++ b/lib/config.hin
@@ -2586,10 +2586,10 @@
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC
 #endif
 
-#if 201710L < __STDC_VERSION__
-# define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD [[__nodiscard__]]
-#elif _GL_HAS_ATTRIBUTE (warn_unused_result)
+#if _GL_HAS_ATTRIBUTE (warn_unused_result)
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD __attribute__ ((__warn_unused_result__))
+#elif 201710L < __STDC_VERSION__
+# define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD [[__nodiscard__]]
 #else
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD
 #endif
-- 
2.47.1
